{"abstract":"Multiparty session types is a typing discipline used to write specifications, known as global types, for branching and recursive message-passing systems. A necessary operation on global types is projection to abstractions of local behaviour, called local types. Typically, this is a computable partial function that given a global type and a role erases all details irrelevant to this role. Computable projection functions in the literature are either unsound or too restrictive when dealing with recursion and branching. Recent work has taken a more general approach to projection defining it as a coinductive, but not computable, relation. Our work defines a new computable projection function that is sound and complete with respect to its coinductive counterpart and, hence, equally expressive. All results have been mechanised in the Coq proof assistant.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Tirore, Dawit","Bengtson, Jesper","Carbone, Marco"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-695307"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Coq","Mechanisation","Projection","Session types"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a sound and complete projection for global types","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/opus/volltexte/2023/18403/pdf/LIPIcs-ITP-2023-28.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-695307","identifier":[{"id":"85168768440","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-ed2c6e7a-d23b-4243-8a79-703d470a4895"],"keyword":["Coq","Mechanisation","Projection","Session types"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-5CCB516C5885FDDD1B2BA73762D97C9B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/opus/volltexte/2023/18403/pdf/LIPIcs-ITP-2023-28.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/opus/volltexte/2023/18403/","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Theoretical Computer Science, Programming Logic and Semantics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Dawit","key":"tirorepau","last":"Tirore","locid":"12df9187-47b5-4d7e-87f5-9089a3d229c1","name":"Tirore, Dawit","orcid":"0000-0002-1997-5161","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"bengtsonpau","last":"Bengtson","locid":"b2b68ce2-6257-45bf-ab48-dc17d05c885e","name":"Bengtson, Jesper","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Marco","key":"carbonepau","last":"Carbone","locid":"9027b41a-4159-4db7-9ddd-8fc8f41f1fb3","name":"Carbone, Marco","orcid":"0000-0001-9479-2632","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["18688969"],"journal":"Leibniz International Proceedings in Informatics","publisher":"Schloss Dagstuhl - Leibniz-Zentrum fuer Informatik GmbH","status":"p","title":"Leibniz International Proceedings in Informatics","volume":"268"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85168768440"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-ed2c6e7a-d23b-4243-8a79-703d470a4895"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"A Sound and Complete Projection for Global Types","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-695307","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"A choreography gives a description of how endpoints in a concurrent systems should exchange messages during its execution. In this paper, we informally introduce a choreographic language for describing security protocols and a property language for expressing non-trivial security properties of such protocols. We motivate this work using the envelope protocol [2] as an example, which ensures auditable transfers by means of a TPM, that guarantees that the issuer of a message always learns whether such message has been opened or not. We then take an implementation of the TPM formulated as an API and discuss how such implementation and the usage of the TPM in the protocol can be related. Finally, we illustrate how the protocol and property descriptions can be translated into multiset rewrite rules and metric first order logic respectively, in order to check if auditable transfer holds.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Bruni, Alessandro","Carbone, Marco","Giustolisi, Rosario","Mödersheim, Sebastian Alexander","Schürmann, Carsten"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-310372"],"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Choreography","Security protocols","Verification"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"security protocols as choreographies","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/265046987/Bruni2021_Chapter_SecurityProtocolsAsChoreograph.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-310372","identifier":[{"id":"85119665514","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-13355403-b681-442d-9e5e-d2239d8a164e"],"keyword":["Choreography","Security protocols","Verification"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-0EA9D1A4E0EF8BC005FCFD2FF0A70B10"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/265046987/Bruni2021_Chapter_SecurityProtocolsAsChoreograph.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science, Formal Methods"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Alessandro","key":"brunipau","last":"Bruni","name":"Bruni, Alessandro","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Marco","key":"carbonepau","last":"Carbone","name":"Carbone, Marco","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rosario","key":"giustolisipau","last":"Giustolisi","name":"Giustolisi, Rosario","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Sebastian Alexander","key":"mödersheimpau","last":"Mödersheim","locid":"21eb3855-68a7-4647-a3a0-8526af03169f","name":"Mödersheim, Sebastian Alexander","orcid":"0000-0002-6901-8319","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Carsten","key":"schürmannpau","last":"Schürmann","name":"Schürmann, Carsten","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Daniel","key":"doughertypedh","last":"Dougherty","name":"Dougherty, Daniel","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"José","key":"meseguerpedh","last":"Meseguer","name":"Meseguer, José","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Sebastian Alexander","key":"mödersheimpedh","last":"Mödersheim","name":"Mödersheim, Sebastian Alexander","rank":8,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Paul","key":"rowepedh","last":"Rowe","name":"Rowe, Paul","rank":9,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-030-91631-2_5","isbn":["9783030916305"],"issn":["03029743"],"pages":"98-111","publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p","subtitle":"Essays Dedicated to Joshua Guttman on the Occasion of his 66.66th Birthday","title":"Protocols, Strands, and Logic"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85119665514"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-13355403-b681-442d-9e5e-d2239d8a164e"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Security Protocols as Choreographies","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-310372","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Session types, types for structuring communication between endpoints in distributed systems, are recently being integrated into mainstream programming languages. In practice, a very important notion for dealing with such types is that of subtyping, since it allows for typing larger classes of system, where a program has not precisely the expected behaviour but a similar one. Unfortunately, recent work has shown that subtyping for session types in an asynchronous setting is undecidable. To cope with this negative result, the only approaches we are aware of either restrict the syntax of session types or limit communication (by considering forms of bounded asynchrony). Both approaches are too restrictive in practice, hence we proceed differently by presenting an algorithm for checking subtyping which is sound, but not complete (in some cases it terminates without returning a decisive verdict). The algorithm is based on a tree representation of the coinductive definition of asynchronous subtyping; this tree could be infinite, and the algorithm checks for the presence of finite witnesses of infinite successful subtrees. Furthermore, we provide a tool that implements our algorithm. We use this tool to test our algorithm on many examples that cannot be managed with the previous approaches, and to provide an empirical evaluation of the time and space cost of the algorithm.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Bravetti, Mario","Carbone, Marco","Lange, Julien","Yoshida, Nobuko","Zavattaro, Gianluigi"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381329"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Italy","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Imperial College London","University of Bologna","University of Kent"],"keyword":["Algorithm","Concurrency","Session types","Subtyping"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a sound algorithm for asynchronous session subtyping and its implementation","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.23638/LMCS-17(1:20)2021","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-381329","identifier":[{"id":"85102714387","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-04c5e475-982c-4421-9519-b412d10380e9"],"keyword":["Algorithm","Concurrency","Session types","Subtyping"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-D054BA811EDE110C457919C8C0C12A89"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.23638/LMCS-17(1:20)2021","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"it","key":"university of bologna","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Bologna","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Information Security and Trust","IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Theoretical Computer Science, Programming Logic and Semantics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"gb","key":"university of kent","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Kent","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"gb","key":"imperial college london","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Imperial College London","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mario","key":"bravettipau","last":"Bravetti","name":"Bravetti, Mario","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Marco","key":"carbonepau","last":"Carbone","locid":"9027b41a-4159-4db7-9ddd-8fc8f41f1fb3","name":"Carbone, Marco","orcid":"0000-0001-9479-2632","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Julien","key":"langepau","last":"Lange","name":"Lange, Julien","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Nobuko","key":"yoshidapau","last":"Yoshida","name":"Yoshida, Nobuko","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Gianluigi","key":"zavattaropau","last":"Zavattaro","name":"Zavattaro, Gianluigi","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.23638/lmcs-17(1:20)2021","issn":["18605974"],"issue":"1","journal":"Logical Methods in Computer Science","pages":"1","publisher":"International Federation for Computational Logic","status":"p","title":"Logical Methods in Computer Science","volume":"17"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85102714387"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-04c5e475-982c-4421-9519-b412d10380e9"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"A Sound Algorithm for Asynchronous Session Subtyping and its Implementation","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381329","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"The Convention on Biological Diversity’s post-2020 Global Biodiversity Framework will probably include a goal to stabilize and restore the status of species. Its delivery would be facilitated by making the actions required to halt and reverse species loss spatially explicit. Here, we develop a species threat abatement and restoration (STAR) metric that is scalable across species, threats and geographies. STAR quantifies the contributions that abating threats and restoring habitats in specific places offer towards reducing extinction risk. While every nation can contribute towards halting biodiversity loss, Indonesia, Colombia, Mexico, Madagascar and Brazil combined have stewardship over 31% of total STAR values for terrestrial amphibians, birds and mammals. Among actions, sustainable crop production and forestry dominate, contributing 41% of total STAR values for these taxonomic groups. Key Biodiversity Areas cover 9% of the terrestrial surface but capture 47% of STAR values. STAR could support governmental and non-state actors in quantifying their contributions to meeting science-based species targets within the framework.","author_count":88,"contributors":["Mair, Louise","Bennun, Leon A.","Brooks, Thomas M.","Butchart, Stuart H. M.","Bolam, Friederike C.","Burgess, Neil David","Ekstrom, Jonathan M. M.","Milner-Gulland, E. J.","Hoffmann, Michael","Ma, Keping","Macfarlane, Nicholas B. W.","Raimondo, Domitilla C.","Rodrigues, Ana S. L.","Shen, Xiaoli","Strassburg, Bernardo B. N.","Beatty, Craig R.","Gómez-Creutzberg, Carla","Iribarrem, Alvaro","Irmadhiany, Meizani","Lacerda, Eduardo","Mattos, Bianca C.","Parakkasi, Karmila","Tognelli, Marcelo F.","Bennett, Elizabeth L.","Bryan, Catherine","Carbone, Giulia","Chaudhary, Abhishek","Eiselin, Maxime","da Fonseca, Gustavo A. B.","Galt, Russell","Geschke, Arne","Glew, Louise","Goedicke, Romie","Green, Jonathan M. H.","Gregory, Richard D.","Hill, Samantha L. L.","Hole, David G.","Hughes, Jonathan","Hutton, Jonat