{"abstract":"We provide the first formal model for declarative choreographies, which is able to express general omega-regular liveness properties. We use the Dynamic Condition Response (DCR) graphs notation for both choreographies and end-points. We define end-point projection as a restriction of DCR graphs and derive the condition for end-point projectability from the causal relationships of the graph. We illustrate the results with a running example of a Buyer-Seller-Shipper protocol. All the examples are available for simulation in the online DCR workbench at http://dcr.tools/forte19.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Hildebrandt, Thomas T.","Slaats, Tijs","López, Hugo A.","Debois, Søren","Carbone, Marco"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382348"],"event":{"acronym":"FORTE","title":"International Conference on Formal Techniques for Distributed Objects, Components, and Systems"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Choreographies","Declarative models","Liveness"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"declarative choreographies and liveness","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/84259682/DeclarativeChoreographies_2_.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-382348","identifier":[{"id":"85067365596","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-486fbcd3-85c7-42d1-9a66-809e6ade54d9"],"keyword":["Choreographies","Declarative models","Liveness"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-5-4192F8BEA87681AD39220F45040EF23B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/84259682/DeclarativeChoreographies_2_.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Theoretical Computer Science, Programming Logic and Semantics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas T.","key":"hildebrandtpau","last":"Hildebrandt","name":"Hildebrandt, Thomas T.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Tijs","key":"slaatspau","last":"Slaats","name":"Slaats, Tijs","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Hugo A.","key":"lópezpau","last":"López","name":"López, Hugo A.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren","key":"deboispau","last":"Debois","name":"Debois, Søren","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Marco","key":"carbonepau","last":"Carbone","locid":"9027b41a-4159-4db7-9ddd-8fc8f41f1fb3","name":"Carbone, Marco","orcid":"0000-0001-9479-2632","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-030-21759-4_8","eisbn":["9783030217594"],"issn":["03029743"],"pages":"129-147","publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p","subtitle":"FORTE 2019: Formal Techniques for Distributed Objects, Components, and Systems","title":"International Conference on Formal Techniques for Distributed Objects, Components, and Systems"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85067365596"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-486fbcd3-85c7-42d1-9a66-809e6ade54d9"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Declarative Choreographies and Liveness","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382348","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Session types, types for structuring communication between endpoints in distributed systems, are recently being integrated into mainstream programming languages. In practice, a very important notion for dealing with such types is that of subtyping, since it allows for typing larger classes of system, where a program has not precisely the expected behavior but a similar one. Unfortunately, recent work has shown that subtyping for session types in an asynchronous setting is undecidable. To cope with this negative result, the only approaches we are aware of either restrict the syntax of session types or limit communication (by considering forms of bounded asynchrony). Both approaches are too restrictive in practice, hence we proceed differently by presenting an algorithm for checking subtyping which is sound, but not complete (in some cases it terminates without returning a decisive verdict). The algorithm is based on a tree representation of the coinductive definition of asynchronous subtyping; this tree could be infinite, and the algorithm checks for the presence of finite witnesses of infinite successful subtrees. Furthermore, we provide a tool that implements our algorithm and we apply it to many examples that cannot be managed with the previous approaches.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Bravetti, Mario","Carbone, Marco","Lange, Julien","Yoshida, Nobuko","Zavattaro, Gianluigi"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383464"],"event":{"acronym":"CONCUR","title":"International Conference on Concurrency Theory"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Italy","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Imperial College London","University of Bologna","University of Kent"],"keyword":["Algorithm for Subtyping","Asynchronous communication","Distributed systems","Session types","Subtyping"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a sound algorithm for asynchronous session subtyping","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4230/LIPIcs.CONCUR.2019.34","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383464","identifier":[{"id":"85071618264","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-959edafa-a77e-414d-b693-8f855016cfee"],"keyword":["Algorithm for Subtyping","Asynchronous Communication","Distributed Systems","Session Types","Subtyping"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-018F9156C1FB3A5B20A41518565672C0"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4230/LIPIcs.CONCUR.2019.34","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/84834004/main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/1907.00421","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"it","key":"university of bologna","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Bologna","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Information Security and Trust","IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Theoretical Computer Science, Programming Logic and Semantics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"gb","key":"university of kent","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Kent","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"gb","key":"imperial college london","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Imperial College London","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mario","key":"bravettipau","last":"Bravetti","name":"Bravetti, Mario","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Marco","key":"carbonepau","last":"Carbone","locid":"9027b41a-4159-4db7-9ddd-8fc8f41f1fb3","name":"Carbone, Marco","orcid":"0000-0001-9479-2632","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Julien","key":"langepau","last":"Lange","name":"Lange, Julien","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Nobuko","key":"yoshidapau","last":"Yoshida","name":"Yoshida, Nobuko","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Gianluigi","key":"zavattaropau","last":"Zavattaro","name":"Zavattaro, Gianluigi","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.4230/lipics.concur.2019.34","issn":["18688969"],"journal":"Leibniz International Proceedings in Informatics","publisher":"Schloss Dagstuhl - Leibniz-Zentrum fuer Informatik GmbH","status":"p","title":"Leibniz International Proceedings in Informatics","volume":"140"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85071618264"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-959edafa-a77e-414d-b693-8f855016cfee"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"A Sound Algorithm for Asynchronous Session Subtyping","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383464","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"We present Multiparty Classical Choreographies (MCC), a language model where global descriptions of communicating systems (choreographies) implement typed multiparty sessions. Typing is achieved by generalising classical linear logic to judgements that explicitly record parallelism by means of hypersequents. Our approach unifies different lines of work on choreographies and processes with multiparty sessions, as well as their connection to linear logic. Thus, results developed in one context are carried over to the others. Key novelties of MCC include support for server invocation in choreographies, as well as logic-driven compilation of choreographies with replicated processes.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Carbone, Marco","Cruz-Filipe, Luís","Montesi, Fabrizio","Murawska, Agata"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-606994"],"event":{"acronym":"LOPSTR","end":"2018-09-06","place":"Frankfurt, de","start":"2018-09-04","title":"28th International Symposium on Logic-Based Program Synthesis and Transformation, LOPSTR 2018","year":"2018"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Carbone, Marco"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"multiparty classical choreographies","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1808.05088.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-606994","identifier":[{"id":"85064049666","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-761616b7-5223-435c-8664-1be02c302e2e"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-4FF7E088212ABBC14B4D078B553295A3"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1808.05088.pdf","versio