{"abstract":"We present Multiparty Classical Choreographies (MCC), a language model where global descriptions of communicating systems (choreographies) implement typed multiparty sessions. Typing is achieved by generalising classical linear logic to judgements that explicitly record parallelism by means of hypersequents. Our approach unifies different lines of work on choreographies and processes with multiparty sessions, as well as their connection to linear logic. Thus, results developed in one context are carried over to the others. Key novelties of MCC include support for server invocation in choreographies, as well as logic-driven compilation of choreographies with replicated processes.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Carbone, Marco","Cruz-Filipe, Luı́s","Montesi, Fabrizio","Murawska, Agata Anna"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384267"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Classical Linear Logic","Multiparty Classical Choreographies","hypersequents","server invocation in choreographies","typed multiparty sessions"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"multparty classical choreographies","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/1808.05088","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384267","ids":["itu-cd02b397-63b3-4755-bf19-ebd06a13f9fa"],"keyword":["Multiparty Classical Choreographies","classical linear logic","hypersequents","server invocation in choreographies","typed multiparty sessions"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-1F7A0C69B5D440E961FBB589BE99AD8C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/1808.05088","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1808.05088.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Theoretical Computer Science, Programming Logic and Semantics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["University of Southern Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Marco","key":"carbonepau","last":"Carbone","locid":"9027b41a-4159-4db7-9ddd-8fc8f41f1fb3","name":"Carbone, Marco","orcid":"0000-0001-9479-2632","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Luı́s","key":"cruzfilipepau","last":"Cruz-Filipe","name":"Cruz-Filipe, Luı́s","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Fabrizio","key":"montesipau","last":"Montesi","name":"Montesi, Fabrizio","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Agata Anna","key":"murawskapau","last":"Murawska","name":"Murawska, Agata Anna","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-cd02b397-63b3-4755-bf19-ebd06a13f9fa"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Multparty Classical Choreographies","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384267","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Autoimmune liver diseases (AILDs) are complex conditions, which arise from the interaction between a genetic susceptibility and unknown environmental triggers. They represent a relevant cause of liver failure and liver transplantation worldwide. As a testimony of our progress in understanding the biology of AILDs and the disease progression is the overall median survival which has increased over the last decade. However, there are still major challenges such as the lack of therapies and surveillance strategies in primary sclerosing cholangitis (PSC), the management and treatment of non-responders to first-line therapies in primary biliary cholangitis (PBC) and the need for tailoring immunosuppressive drugs in autoimmune hepatitis (AIH). The different disease course and treatment response in patients with AILDs might be related to a heterogeneous genetic background between individuals which translates in a heterogeneous clinical phenotype. Thus, it becomes essential to personalise management and treatment based on specific risk profiles, e.g. low-risk and high-risk, based on genetic and molecular signatures. It is now possible, thanks to the development of large-scale AILDs patient cohorts, that such diseases can be analysed using various high-throughput methods like gene expression profiling, next generation sequencing and other omics technologies to identify unique fingerprints based on which a personalised or tailor-made management and therapy can be developed. The final aim being to facilitate treatment decision-making that balances patient-specific risks and preferences. This is critical especially now with the current and forthcoming availability of more efficacious medications. To reach this point we need specific interventions such as creating bigger biobanks, sequencing more genomes and linking biological information to health-related data. We have already identified subsets of patients with different risk profiles among patients with PBC, PSC and AIH by using clinical tools such as liver histology, laboratory investigation and non-invasive methods. In this manuscript, we review the clinical features and investigations that already enable us to individualize the care of PBC patients and that might support the development of precision medicine (PM) in AILDs.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Bossen, Lars","Gerussi, Alessio","Lygoura, Vasiliki","Mells, George F","Carbone, Marco","Invernizzi, Pietro"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-223786"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Italy","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Cambridge","University of Milan","University of Milan - Bicocca"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"support of precision medicine through risk stratification in autoimmune liver diseases histology scoring systems and non invasive markers","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"djr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85049922281","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-223786","identifier":[{"id":"30005861","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85049922281","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-a5b53c78-452e-4b3e-b4ef-b23db10fd196"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-F62E542EF9E70C33E34C9FC14264D1AD"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Hepatology and Gastroenterology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"it","key":"university of milan bicocca","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Milan - Bicocca","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"gb","key":"university of cambridge","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Cambridge","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"it","key":"university of milan","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Milan","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars","key":"bossenpau","last":"Bossen","locid":"c408b4e3-ce19-4be5-8614-e5cfee7d7b23","name":"Bossen, Lars","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Alessio","key":"gerussipau","last":"Gerussi","name":"Gerussi, Alessio","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Vasiliki","key":"lygourapau","last":"Lygoura","name":"Lygoura, Vasiliki","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"George F","key":"mellspau","last":"Mells","name":"Mells, George F","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Marco","key":"carbonepau","last":"Carbone","name":"Carbone, Marco","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Pietro","key":"invernizzipau","last":"Invernizzi","name":"Invernizzi, Pietro","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["30005861"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.autrev.2018.02.013","issn":["15689972","18730183"],"issn_org":["15689972"],"issue":"9","journal":"Autoimmunity Reviews","pages":"854-865","publisher":"Elsevier BV","publisher_org":"Elsevier B.V.","status":"p","title":"Autoimmunity Reviews","volume":"17"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85049922281"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-a5b53c78-452e-4b