LOI:S01-000.00-198202","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Session types are used to describe communication protocols in distributed systems and, as usual in type theories, session subtyping characterizes substitutability of the communicating processes. We investigate the (un)decidability of subtyping for session types in asynchronously communicating systems. We first devise a core undecidable subtyping relation that is obtained by imposing limitations on the structure of types. Then, as a consequence of this initial undecidability result, we show that (differently from what stated or conjectured in the literature) the three notions of asynchronous subtyping defined so far for session types are all undecidable. Namely, we consider the asynchronous session subtyping by Mostrous and Yoshida for binary sessions, the relation by Chen et al. for binary sessions under the assumption that every message emitted is eventually consumed, and the one by Mostrous et al. for multiparty session types. Finally, by showing that two fragments of the core subtyping relation are decidable, we evince that further restrictions on the structure of types make our core subtyping relation decidable.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Bravetti, Mario","Carbone, Marco","Zavattaro, Gianluigi"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382879"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Italy"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Bologna"],"keyword":["Queue Machines","Session types","Subtyping","Undecidability"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"undecidability of asynchronous session subtyping","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82422584/main.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-382879","identifier":[{"id":"85026420735","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-6c1eaf6f-6be1-40e8-92d4-088a667fa323"],"keyword":["Queue Machines","Session Types","Subtyping","Undecidability"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-505532F1B64424AD8F58B2E094F385EA"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82422584/main.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"it","key":"university of bologna","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Bologna","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Theoretical Computer Science, Programming Logic and Semantics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mario","key":"bravettipau","last":"Bravetti","name":"Bravetti, Mario","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Marco","key":"carbonepau","last":"Carbone","locid":"9027b41a-4159-4db7-9ddd-8fc8f41f1fb3","name":"Carbone, Marco","orcid":"0000-0001-9479-2632","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Gianluigi","key":"zavattaropau","last":"Zavattaro","name":"Zavattaro, Gianluigi","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.ic.2017.07.010","issn":["08905401","10902651"],"issn_org":["08905401"],"journal":"Information and Computation","pages":"300-320","publisher":"Academic Press","status":"p","title":"Information and Computation","volume":"256"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85026420735"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-6c1eaf6f-6be1-40e8-92d4-088a667fa323"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Undecidability of asynchronous session subtyping","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382879","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"We propose a Curry–Howard correspondence between a language for programming multiparty sessions and a generalisation of Classical Linear Logic (CLL). In this framework, propositions correspond to the local behaviour of a participant in a multiparty session type, proofs to processes, and proof normalisation to executing communications. Our key contribution is generalising duality, from CLL, to a new notion of n-ary compatibility, called coherence. Building on coherence as a principle of compositionality, we generalise the cut rule of CLL to a new rule for composing many processes communicating in a multiparty session. We prove the soundness of our model by showing the admissibility of our new rule, which entails deadlock-freedom via our correspondence.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Carbone, Marco","Montesi, Fabrizio","Montesi, Fabrizio","Schürmann, Carsten","Yoshida, Nobuko"],"cuid":["S02-097.45-038362"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Montesi, Fabrizio"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Imperial College London"],"keyword":["Linear Logic","Local Type","Parallel Composition","Proof System","Proof theory"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"multiparty session types as coherence proofs","src":["itu","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/83025669/Multiparty_session_types_as_coherence_proofs.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["We thank Kim Skak Larsen and the anonymous reviewers for their useful comments. Montesi was supported by CRC (Choreographies for Reliable and efficient Communication software), grant no. DFF?4005-00304 from the Danish Council for Independent Research. Sch?rmann was partly supported by DemTech, grant no. 10-092309 from the Danish Council for Strategic Research. Yoshida was partially sponsored by the EPSRC EP/K011715/1, EP/K034413/1, EP/L00058X/1, and EU project FP7-612985 UpScale. This work is also supported by the COST Action IC1201 BETTY."],"id":"S02-097.45-038362","identifier":[{"id":"84995495349","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-aac6755a-e508-4671-ba1e-88386a79257f","sdu-bf18d070-2ef5-4420-841b-91846e2af61c"],"keyword":["Linear Logic","Local Type","Parallel Composition","Proof System","Proof Theory"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-3D19E5F63DE3E53231AC750CA4F4C496"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/83025669/Multiparty_session_types_as_coherence_proofs.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Theoretical Computer Science, Programming Logic and Semantics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Mathematics and Computer Science","SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Mathematics and Computer Science, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"gb","key":"imperial college london","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Imperial College London","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Marco","key":"carbonemarcopau","last":"Carbone","locid":"9027b41a-4159-4db7-9ddd-8fc8f41f1fb3","name":"Carbone, Marco","orcid":"0000-0001-9479-2632","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Fabrizio","key":"montesifabriziopau","last":"Montesi","locid":"81d9220c-ba43-48b1-aa21-129c942a9c92","name":"Montesi, Fabrizio","orcid":"0000-0003-4666-901X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Carsten","key":"schürmanncarstenpau","last":"Schürmann","locid":"1313519f-2074-41d6-8b79-589648e37211","name":"Schürmann, Carsten","orcid":"0000-0003-4793-0099","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Nobuko","key":"yoshidanobukopau","last":"Yoshida","name":"Yoshida, Nobuko","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s00236-016-0285-y","issn":["00015903","14320525"],"issn_org":["00015903"],"issue":"3","journal":"Acta Informatica","pages":"243-269","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"Acta Informatica","volume":"54"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84995495349"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-aac6755a-e508-4671-ba1e-88386a79257f","sdu-bf18d070-2ef5-4420-841b-91846e2af61c"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Multiparty session types as coherence proofs","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-097.45-038362","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Metal-polluted mine waters represent a major threat to the quality of waters and sediments in a downstream basin. At the confluence between acidic mine waters and the unpolluted waters of the Gromolo Torrent (Liguria, North-West Italy), the massive formation of an ochreous amorphous precipitate takes place. This precipitate forms a soft blanket that covers the torrent bed and can be observed down to its mouth in the sea. The aim of this work is to evaluate the dispersion of metals in the Gromolo Torrent basin from the abandoned Cu-Fe sulphide mine of Libiola to the Ligurian Sea and to assess the metal remobilisation from the amorphous precipitates. The mineralogy of the superficial sediments collected in the torrent bed and the concentrations of different elements of environmental concern (Cu, Zn, Cd, Co, Cr, Mn, Ni, Pb, As, and Sb) were therefore analysed. The results showed that the precipitates contain high concentration of Fe, Al, Cu, and Zn, significantly modifying the bulk chemistry of the Gromolo Torrent sediments. In order to evaluate the possible remobilisation of ecotoxic elements from the amorphous precipitates, bulk leaching tests were performed with both deionised and seawater. Bulk leaching tests with deionised water mobilised primarily high Pb amounts, but also relatively high concentrations of Fe, Al, Cu, and Zn are released in the leachate. In seawater tests, Fe, Al, Cu, and Zn were released in smaller amounts, while other elements like Mn, Cd, Co, and Ni increased in the released fraction. Pb was still strongly released as in deionised water experiments. The results show that the interaction of precipitates and seawater can remobilise high concentrations of metals, thus affecting the surrounding environment.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Consani, Sirio","Carbone, Cristina","Dinelli, Enrico","Balic Zunic, Tonci","Cutroneo, Laura","Capello, Marco","Salviulo, Gabriella","Lucchetti, Gabriella"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-451019"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Italy"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Bologna","University of Genoa","University of Padua"],"keyword":["Acid mine drainage AMD","Environmental contamination"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"metal transport and remobilisation in a basin affected by acid mine drainage the role of ochreous amorphous precipitates","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-451019","identifier":[{"id":"85019642690","type":"scopus"},{"id":"28528499","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-603708e2-5aca-4618-9dae-ce51088b8947"],"keyword":["Acid mine drainage (AMD)","Amorphous precipitates","Bulk leaching tests","Environmental contamination","Libiola mine","Metal mobility"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-C60B3EEB8562EB25FD42297E829C2752"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"it","key":"university of genoa","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Genoa","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"it","key":"university of bologna","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Bologna","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Geosciences and Natural Resource Management, Geology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"it","key":"university of padua","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Padua","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Sirio","key":"consanipau","last":"Consani","name":"Consani, Sirio","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Cristina","key":"carbonepau","last":"Carbone","name":"Carbone, Cristina","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Enrico","key":"dinellipau","last":"Dinelli","name":"Dinelli, Enrico","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Tonci","key":"baliczunicpau","last":"Balic Zunic","locid":"73e85088-cae0-4517-b2cf-9f339afd3c59","name":"Balic Zunic, Tonci","orcid":"0000-0003-1687-1233","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Laura","key":"cutroneopau","last":"Cutroneo","name":"Cutroneo, Laura","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Marco","key":"capellopau","last":"Capello","name":"Capello, Marco","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Gabriella","key":"salviulopau","last":"Salviulo","name":"Salviulo, Gabriella","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Gabriella","key":"lucchettipau","last":"Lucchetti","name":"Lucchetti, Gabriella","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["28528499"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s11356-017-9209-9","issn":["09441344","16147499"],"issn_org":["09441344"],"issue":"18","journal":"Environmental Science and Pollution Research","pages":"15735-15747","status":"p","title":"Environmental Science and Pollution Research","volume":"24"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85019642690"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-603708e2-5aca-4618-9dae-ce51088b8947"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Metal transport and remobilisation in a basin affected by acid mine drainage : the role of ochreous amorphous precipitates","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-451019","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Communication is a central elements in software development. As a potential typed foundation for structured communication-centered programming, session types have been studied over the past decade for a wide range of process calculi and programming languages, focusing on binary (two-party) sessions. This work extends the foregoing theories of binary session types to multiparty, asynchronous sessions, which often arise in practical communication-centered applications. Presented as a typed calculus for mobile processes, the theory introduces a new notion of types in which interactions involving multiple peers are directly abstracted as a global scenario. Global types retain the friendly type syntax of binary session types while specifying dependencies and capturing complex causal chains of multiparty asynchronous interactions. A global type plays the role of a shared agreement among communication peers and is used as a basis of efficient type-checking through its projection onto individual peers. The fundamental properties of the session type discipline, such as communication safety, progress, and session fidelity, are established for general n-party asynchronous interactions.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Honda, Kohei","Yoshida, Nobuko","Carbone, Marco"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384817"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Imperial College London","Queen Mary University of London"],"keyword":["Progress","Projection","Session types","global protocols","global types","the pi calculus"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"multiparty asynchronous session types","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/83523575/a9_honda.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384817","identifier":[{"id":"84968817456","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-f154b152-abd3-4f1e-a5d5-c0825f87ebd4"],"keyword":["Session types","global protocols","global types","progress","projection","the pi-calculus"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-26F689E30713E4CC1BB881C9B58074F5"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/83523575/a9_honda.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"gb","key":"queen mary university of london","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Queen Mary University of London","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gb","key":"imperial college london","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Imperial College London","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Theoretical Computer Science, Programming Logic and Semantics","The Department, Theoretical Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kohei","key":"hondapau","last":"Honda","name":"Honda, Kohei","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Nobuko","key":"yoshidapau","last":"Yoshida","name":"Yoshida, Nobuko","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Marco","key":"carbonepau","last":"Carbone","locid":"9027b41a-4159-4db7-9ddd-8fc8f41f1fb3","name":"Carbone, Marco","orcid":"0000-0001-9479-2632","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/2827695","issn":["00045411","1557735X"],"issn_org":["00045411"],"issue":"1","journal":"Journal of the ACM","pages":"1","paperid":"9","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"Journal of the ACM","volume":"63"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84968817456"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-f154b152-abd3-4f1e-a5d5-c0825f87ebd4"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Multiparty Asynchronous Session Types","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384817","year":"2016","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Behavioural type systems, usually associated to concurrent or distributed computations, encompass concepts such as interfaces, communication protocols, and contracts, in addition to the traditional input/output operations. The behavioural type of a software component specifies its expected patterns of interaction using expressive type languages, so types can be used to determine automatically whether the component interacts correctly with other components. Two related important notions of behavioural types are those of session types and behavioural contracts. This article surveys the main accomplishments of the last 20 years within these two approaches.","author_count":16,"contributors":["Hüttel, Hans","Lanese, Ivan","T. Vasconcelos, Vasco","Caires, Luis","Carbone, Marco","Denielou, Pierre-Malo","Mostrous, Dimitris","Padovani, Luca","Ravara, Antonia","Tuosto, Emilio","Torres Vieira, Hugo","Zavattaro, Gainluigi"],"cuid":["S02-092.24-009804"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Italy","Portugal","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","IMT School for Advanced Studies Lucca","NOVA University Lisbon","Royal Holloway, University of London","University Institute of Lisbon","University of Bologna","University of Leicester","University of Lisbon","University of London","University of Turin"],"keyword":["Behavioural types","Language Constructs and Features","Software Program Verification"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"foundations of session types and behavioural contracts","src":["aau","itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license"