Viganò","name":"Viganò, Luca","rank":22,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-642-28756-5_19","eisbn":["9783642287565"],"isbn":["9783642287558"],"issn":["03029743"],"pages":"267-282","publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p","subtitle":"18th International Conference, TACAS 2012, Held as Part of the European Joint Conferences on Theory and Practice of Software, ETAPS 2012, Tallinn, Estonia, March 24 – April 1, 2012. Proceedings","title":"Tools and Algorithms for the Construction and Analysis of Systems"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84859336099"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-0ec81d2e-644c-44b4-8288-cba8c7e31f56"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"The AVANTSSAR Platform for the Automated Validation of Trust and Security of Service-Oriented Architectures","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-309034","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"This article relates two different paradigms of descriptions of communication behavior, one focusing on global message flows and another on end-point behaviors, using formal calculi based on session types. The global calculus, which originates from a Web service description language (W3C WS-CDL), describes an interaction scenario from a vantage viewpoint; the end-point calculus, an applied typed π -calculus, precisely identifies a local behavior of each participant. We explore a theory of end-point projection, by which we can map a global description to its end-point counterparts preserving types and dynamics. Three principles of well-structured description and the type structures play a fundamental role in the theory.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Carbone, Marco","Honda, Kohei","Yoshida, Nobuko"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382651"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Imperial College London","Queen Mary University of London"],"keyword":["Choreography","Communication","Process calculi","Session types","Web services","end point projection","type system"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"structured communication centered programming for web services","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/37386331/a8_carbone_1.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-382651","identifier":[{"id":"84866017941","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-5c6869fc-6df4-4738-ae52-40380af83c37"],"keyword":["Communication","choreography","end-point projection","process calculi","session types","type system","web services"],"lang":"Engli